"use strict";
window.LC_CHUNKS=window.LC_CHUNKS||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"]=window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"]||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"][35]={"university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M35-L1":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L1\">M35-L1 – Embedded Control under Timing Constraints: Latency Paths and Test Strategies<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M35 – Master: Time-critical Embedded Control<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Master · Master’s Specialisation<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M13&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M13-L5<\/a>,\n<a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M28&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M28-L4<\/a>,\n<a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M16&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M16-L3<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Record deadline misses, overload\nand sampling delay separately, and justify test strategies.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>From measurement time to control output<\/h2>\n<p>Discrete-time control requires not only a correct computational\nfunction but also the correct timing. Acquisition, transfer, scheduling,\ncomputation time and waiting for output all occur between the physical\nmeasurement time and actuator output. The term latency therefore\nrequires defined start and end points. For a block collected in the\npreceding sampling window, the oldest data are already older than the\nnewest data at the release time.<\/p>\n<p>In the nominal project, let the last measured value be available at\ntime\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>k<\/mi><mi>P<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r_k=kP<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe output deadline is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi>D<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r_k+D<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe start of execution,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>s<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nmay be later because an earlier job is still running. With service time\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand completion time\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nwe have<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>s<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>W<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>s<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_k=s_k+C_k,\\qquad R_k=f_k-r_k,\\qquad W_k=s_k-r_k.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>For accepted jobs,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>W<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_k=W_k+C_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nA dropped job has no\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand must therefore be counted neither as zero latency nor as a\nsuccessful job. The deadline is met when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>≤<\/mo><msub><mi>r<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi>D<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_k\\le r_k+D<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>;\na later completion is late in the model even if the calculated value is\ncorrect.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_106_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Release, queue, completion and deadline, and implications for the control loop.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Waiting and service time lie between job release and\ncompletion; a delayed start can cause the control chain to miss its\ndeadline despite short actual compute time.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Timing budget and control-loop dynamics<\/h2>\n<p>A constant delay\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>τ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmultiplies the transfer function in the frequency domain by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>e<\/mi><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><mi>ω<\/mi><mi>τ<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{-j\\omega\\tau}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe magnitude remains one and the additional phase is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mi>ω<\/mi><mi>τ<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\omega\\tau<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nAt 100 Hz and 555 µs, this amounts to approximately −20.0°; at 218 µs,\napproximately −7.85°. This calculation concerns processing latency\nalone, not the entire loop including sampling and the hold element. At\nthe same frequency, an additional delay of 350 µs would contribute a\nfurther −12.6°. Whether the control loop remains stable depends on the\nplant, controller design and all delay paths. Variable delays and\ndropouts cannot generally be represented by a single phase angle.<\/p>\n<p>A linear discrete-time model with a delay of one complete time step\ncan, for example, be described by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>a<\/mi><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><msub><mi>u<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{k+1}=a x_k+b u_{k-1}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe unavailable current control output is accounted for by an additional\nstate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>u<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_k=u_{k-1}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>u<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z_{k+1}=u_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mi>K<\/mi><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_k=-Kx_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthis yields<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" class=\"text-center\"><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mtd><\/mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" class=\"text-center\"><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mtd><\/mtr><\/mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><mo>=<\/mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" class=\"text-center\"><mi>a<\/mi><\/mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" class=\"text-center\"><mi>b<\/mi><\/mtd><\/mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" class=\"text-center\"><mi>−<\/mi><mi>K<\/mi><\/mtd><mtd columnalign=\"center\" class=\"text-center\"><mn>0<\/mn><\/mtd><\/mtr><\/mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" class=\"text-center\"><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mtd><\/mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"center\" class=\"text-center\"><msub><mi>z<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><\/mtd><\/mtr><\/mtable><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\begin{bmatrix}x_{k+1}\\\\z_{k+1}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\\\-K&amp;0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x_k\\\\z_k\\end{bmatrix}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=0.9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b=0.2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe pole without delay is −0.1; with a delay of one time step,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ<\/mi><mn>2<\/mn><\/msup><mo>−<\/mo><mn>0.9<\/mn><mi>λ<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda^2-0.9\\lambda+1=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>:\nboth complex poles have magnitude 1. The example is marginally stable in\nthe ideal linear model, not asymptotically stable. <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M35&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M35-L2<\/a>,\non the other hand, simulates the processing chain rather than a physical\nplant; such a stability analysis would be a subsequent experiment in its\nown right.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Overload and monitoring<\/h2>\n<p>For a periodic serial server with constant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>C<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mi>C<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P&lt;C<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe backlog increases by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>P<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C-P<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nper job until the buffer is full. With two job slots, including the\nactive job, sustained overload leads to dropped jobs. The choice of\nstrategy (oldest or newest job, coalescing, safe fallback value) is a\nsystem requirement. <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M35&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M35-L2<\/a>\nuses drop-new, that is, dropping the new job when the buffer is full.\nThis is not automatically the best control strategy, since older data\nmay remain in effect for longer.<\/p>\n<p>A watchdog and a control output subjected to plausibility checks may\nform part of fault management. For safety-critical functions, the output\npermitted when measurement data are stale must be specified\nindependently. Testing the deadline alone is then insufficient.\nActivation delay, priority inversion, bus arbitration and unfavourable\ncache states must also be considered. For fixed priorities and\nindependent periodic tasks on a preemptive single core, a classical\nresponse-time iteration is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mo>∑<\/mo><mrow><mi>j<\/mi><mo>∈<\/mo><mi>h<\/mi><mi>p<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>i<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">⌈<\/mo><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">⌉<\/mo><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_i=C_i+B_i+\\sum_{j\\in hp(i)}\\lceil R_i/T_j\\rceil C_j<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nunder suitable modelling assumptions. With\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_i=2<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B_i=0.5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\none higher-priority task with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_j=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mi>j<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_j=4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\n(all in ms), the iteration converges to 3.5 ms. Bus and multicore\neffects require additional treatment.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Test plan<\/h2>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-50\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-50\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Test<\/th>\n<th>Purpose<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Nominal load<\/td>\n<td>Compare values and response times against the reference<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Interfering CPU load<\/td>\n<td>Scheduling and waiting-time effects<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Interfering bus load<\/td>\n<td>Reveal a transfer bottleneck<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Increased release rate<\/td>\n<td>Throughput and buffer occupancy<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Overload<\/td>\n<td>Count dropped jobs and verify recovery<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Combined conditions<\/td>\n<td>Interaction between waiting times and deadlines<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>Record release and completion timestamps in a common time base, along\nwith sequence numbers. A timing instrument, logger or tracing may itself\nalter behaviour and must be calibrated. The maximum measured latency is\nonly a lower bound on the unknown worst-case latency; deterministic\nguarantees require a sound timing model or other suitable evidence.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Exercises and review<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Release at 1000 µs, start at 1200 µs, service time 550 µs and\ndeadline 700 µs after release. <strong>Solution:<\/strong> response time\n750 µs, thus 50 µs late.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Calculate the phase of a pure delay of 1 ms at 50 Hz.\n<strong>Solution:<\/strong> −18°.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why should the mean latency of completed jobs alone not be used as a\nsuccess metric for an overloaded system? <strong>Solution:<\/strong>\ndropped jobs are absent from the sample; aggressive dropping could\nimprove the mean even though the function deteriorates.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.vvz.ethz.ch/Vorlesungsverzeichnis/sucheLehrangebot.view?abschnittId=122815&amp;ansicht=1&amp;lang=en&amp;seite=0&amp;semkez=2026W\">ETH\nZürich – Computers and Networks (Curriculum G5)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Autumn 2026,\nComputers and Networks track: 227-0124-00L Embedded Systems; curricular\ncomparison only, no proof of individual equations or experiment. · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://idsc.ethz.ch/education/lectures/embedded-control-systems.html\">ETH\nZürich – Embedded Control Systems, Institute for Dynamic Systems and\nControl<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Abstract and Subjects covered in lectures and practical\nlab exercises: sampling, ADC and timer interrupts; curricular context,\nnot evidence of project results. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-004-computation-structures-spring-2009/pages/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nOCW – 6.004, Lecture Notes: Pipelining, Memory Hierarchy, Parallel\nProcessing<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Lectures 8, 15–16, 19, 22–24: latency, memory\nhierarchy, interrupts and pipelining; no experiment validation. · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M35-L2":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L2\">M35-L2 – Specialisation Project: Measuring and Comparing Two Architectures for a Sensor–Controller Chain<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M35 – Master: Time-critical Embedded Control<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Master · Master’s Specialisation<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M16&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M16-L3<\/a>,\n<a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M34&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M34-L5<\/a>,\n<a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M35&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M35-L1<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Reproducibly compare two\narchitecture models with identical inputs and separate timing, loss and\nresource metrics.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Project assignment and assumptions<\/h2>\n<p>A virtual sensor supplies a complete block of 64 unsigned 12-bit\nvalues (16-bit storage format) at each release. A simple proportional\ncontrol output is calculated from the integer block mean. Pure CPU\nprocessing is compared with CPU processing using a specialised\naccelerator. The following explicit assumptions constitute a\ndeliberately simplified, deterministic timing model, not a benchmark of\na specific controller. The data represent a synthetic input waveform,\nnot a real measurement or a physical plant under feedback control.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_107_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Maximum response time and on-time responses in the reference model.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Twelve model architecture tests compare worst\nresponse time, CPU demand, deadline misses and data loss; meeting a\ntiming limit does not automatically imply complete data.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<p>The objective under nominal operating conditions is to complete all\n100 jobs without missing a deadline of 700 µs from release, and to\nachieve bit-exact numerical agreement. Under interference or overload,\nlosses and late completions are explicitly evaluated rather than hidden.\nCPU demand, accelerator payload data and completed jobs are separate\nmetrics.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Model boundaries and reference<\/h2>\n<p>Each release contains n=64 values; there are two slots, including the\nblock currently being processed. Both models operate in FIFO order,\nwithout overlap between jobs. If a completion coincides with a new\nrelease, the old slot is freed first. A full buffer discards the new\nrelease. A running job continues to completion even after its deadline;\nafter the final release interval, the buffer is drained. The observation\nduration is the maximum of 100 periods and the final completion\ntime.<\/p>\n<p>For the number\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\mathrm{ok}}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nof on-time responses,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>N<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N_{\\mathrm{ok}}=N_{\\mathrm{fertig}}-N_{\\mathrm{spaet}}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nholds, where the original subscripts fertig and spaet denote completed\nand late jobs. CPU service takes 555 µs, hardware service 218 µs, and\nCPU time on the hardware path is 73 µs. These model values follow from\nthe service function in the program: CPU 25 + 8·64 + 18 = 555 µs;\naccelerator 25 + 20 + 16 + 128 + 10 + 1 + 18 = 218 µs, including 25 + 20\n+ 10 + 18 = 73 µs of CPU work. DMA (direct memory access) denotes the\nmodelled data transfer by a separate unit; bus waiting times are\nadditional model parameters. Every fifth job, starting at index 0, may\nincur additional CPU blocking or additional bus waiting time per DMA\ntransfer. The artificial interference is tied to job indices and is\nmodelled here as additional service time without CPU work of its own. It\nis not a scheduler-accurate operating system model. The displayed CPU\ntime percentages count only modelled useful work, not unrelated CPU\nload. The additional accelerator traffic accounts for 132 payload bytes\nper completed job; CPU and sensor memory traffic are excluded.<\/p>\n<p>The event-based solution stores future completion times of accepted\njobs; the independent reference advances in integer microseconds and\nmaintains an active job and an actual queue. Both use the same timing\nlaw, so they verify the queue implementation, not the physical accuracy\nof the parameters. The numerical CPU sum and the grouped hardware\nreduction are compared separately on identical inputs.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Reproducible Python experiment<\/h2>\n<p>Python 3 with the standard library is sufficient. The 1 µs time grid\nis exact for the integer service times and releases. The simulation does\nnot generate real DMA transactions. <code>COUNT<\/code> and\n<code>Q<\/code> are fixed for the evaluation. Output: completed, dropped,\nlate (among completed jobs), mean and maximum response time in µs,\nuseful CPU time as a percentage, accelerator payload bytes and\nthroughput in jobs/s. The original program is retained; its case labels\nNennbetrieb, CPU-Stoerung, Bus-Stoerung, Hohe Rate, Ueberlast and\nKombiniert correspond to the six English scenario names in the table\nbelow, in that order.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre\nclass=\"sourceCode python\"><code class=\"sourceCode python\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"im\">from<\/span> math <span class=\"im\">import<\/span> ceil, sin, pi<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"im\">from<\/span> statistics <span class=\"im\">import<\/span> mean<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"im\">from<\/span> collections <span class=\"im\">import<\/span> deque<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>N<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">64<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> COUNT<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">100<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> Q<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span>  <span class=\"co\"># including active frame<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"co\"># name, period, deadline (us), CPU blocking every fifth frame, extra DMA time per transfer<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>CASES<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>[(<span class=\"st\">&#39;Nennbetrieb&#39;<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">1000<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">700<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>),(<span class=\"st\">&#39;CPU-Stoerung&#39;<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">1000<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">700<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">350<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>),(<span class=\"st\">&#39;Bus-Stoerung&#39;<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">1000<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">700<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">300<\/span>),(<span class=\"st\">&#39;Hohe Rate&#39;<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">400<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">400<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>),(<span class=\"st\">&#39;Ueberlast&#39;<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">180<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">180<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>),(<span class=\"st\">&#39;Kombiniert&#39;<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">400<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">400<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">150<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">100<\/span>)]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> frame(k):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> [<span class=\"bu\">int<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">2048<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1000<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>sin(<span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>pi<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">64<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>k<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>j)<span class=\"op\">/<\/span><span class=\"dv\">901<\/span>)) <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> j <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">range<\/span>(N)]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> cpu_control(x):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    s<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><a href=\"#cb1-11\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> v <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> x: s<span class=\"op\">+=<\/span>v<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><a href=\"#cb1-12\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">min<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">4095<\/span>,<span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">2048<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">2048<\/span><span class=\"op\">-<\/span>s<span class=\"op\">//<\/span><span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(x))))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><a href=\"#cb1-13\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> accel_control(x):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><a href=\"#cb1-14\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    partial<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>[<span class=\"bu\">sum<\/span>(x[i:i<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>]) <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> i <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">range<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(x),<span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>)]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><a href=\"#cb1-15\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">min<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">4095<\/span>,<span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">6144<\/span><span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>(<span class=\"bu\">sum<\/span>(partial)<span class=\"op\">//<\/span><span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(x))))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><a href=\"#cb1-16\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> service(arch,k,block,bus):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><a href=\"#cb1-17\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    b<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>block <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> k<span class=\"op\">%<\/span><span class=\"dv\">5<\/span><span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> d<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>bus <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> k<span class=\"op\">%<\/span><span class=\"dv\">5<\/span><span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><a href=\"#cb1-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> arch<span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"st\">&#39;CPU&#39;<\/span>: <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">25<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">8<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>N<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">18<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span>b,<span class=\"dv\">25<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">8<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>N<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">18<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><a href=\"#cb1-19\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">25<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">20<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span>ceil(<span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>N<span class=\"op\">/<\/span><span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>)<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>N<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">10<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span>ceil(<span class=\"dv\">4<\/span><span class=\"op\">/<\/span><span class=\"dv\">8<\/span>)<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">18<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span>b<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>d,<span class=\"dv\">25<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">20<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">10<\/span><span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">18<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">2<\/span><span class=\"op\">*<\/span>N<span class=\"op\">+<\/span><span class=\"dv\">4<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-20\"><a href=\"#cb1-20\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-21\"><a href=\"#cb1-21\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> simulate(arch,case):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-22\"><a href=\"#cb1-22\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    _,period,deadline,block,bus<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>case<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> end<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>deque()<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> rows<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>[]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-23\"><a href=\"#cb1-23\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> k <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">range<\/span>(COUNT):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-24\"><a href=\"#cb1-24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        release<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>k<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>period<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-25\"><a href=\"#cb1-25\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">while<\/span> end <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> end[<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span>release: end.popleft()<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-26\"><a href=\"#cb1-26\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(end)<span class=\"op\">&gt;=<\/span>Q: rows.append((k,<span class=\"va\">None<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>,<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>))<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">continue<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-27\"><a href=\"#cb1-27\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        duration,cpu,traffic<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>service(arch,k,block,bus)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-28\"><a href=\"#cb1-28\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        finish<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(release,end[<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>] <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> end <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> release)<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>duration<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> end.append(finish)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-29\"><a href=\"#cb1-29\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        rows.append((k,finish,cpu,traffic))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-30\"><a href=\"#cb1-30\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> rows<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-31\"><a href=\"#cb1-31\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-32\"><a href=\"#cb1-32\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> tick_reference(arch,case):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-33\"><a href=\"#cb1-33\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    _,p,_,block,bus<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>case<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> ready<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>deque()<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> active<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"va\">None<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> finish<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>{}<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> now<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><span class=\"op\">;<\/span> k<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">0<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-34\"><a href=\"#cb1-34\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">while<\/span> k<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span>COUNT <span class=\"kw\">or<\/span> ready <span class=\"kw\">or<\/span> active <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-35\"><a href=\"#cb1-35\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> active <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> active[<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>now:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-36\"><a href=\"#cb1-36\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            finish[active[<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>]]<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>now<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> active<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"va\">None<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-37\"><a href=\"#cb1-37\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> k<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span>COUNT <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> now<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>k<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>p:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-38\"><a href=\"#cb1-38\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(ready)<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>(active <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>)<span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span>Q: ready.append(k)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-39\"><a href=\"#cb1-39\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            k<span class=\"op\">+=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-40\"><a href=\"#cb1-40\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> active <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> ready:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-41\"><a href=\"#cb1-41\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            j<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>ready.popleft()<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> active<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>(j,now<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>service(arch,j,block,bus)[<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>])<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-42\"><a href=\"#cb1-42\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        now<span class=\"op\">+=<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-43\"><a href=\"#cb1-43\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> [finish.get(j) <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> j <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">range<\/span>(COUNT)]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-44\"><a href=\"#cb1-44\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-45\"><a href=\"#cb1-45\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> metrics(rows,case):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-46\"><a href=\"#cb1-46\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    _,p,d,_,_<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>case<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-47\"><a href=\"#cb1-47\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    lat<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>[f<span class=\"op\">-<\/span>k<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>p <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> k,f,_,_ <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> f <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>]<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-48\"><a href=\"#cb1-48\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    dropped<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>COUNT<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(lat)<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> late<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"bu\">sum<\/span>(l<span class=\"op\">&gt;<\/span>d <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> l <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> lat)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-49\"><a href=\"#cb1-49\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    horizon<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(COUNT<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>p,<span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(f <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> _,f,_,_ <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> f <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-50\"><a href=\"#cb1-50\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(lat),dropped,late,mean(lat),<span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(lat),<span class=\"bu\">sum<\/span>(c <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> _,_,c,_ <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows)<span class=\"op\">/<\/span>horizon<span class=\"op\">*<\/span><span class=\"dv\">100<\/span>,<span class=\"bu\">sum<\/span>(b <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> _,_,_,b <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows),<span class=\"bu\">len<\/span>(lat)<span class=\"op\">*<\/span><span class=\"fl\">1e6<\/span><span class=\"op\">/<\/span>horizon<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-51\"><a href=\"#cb1-51\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-52\"><a href=\"#cb1-52\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> <span class=\"va\">__name__<\/span><span class=\"op\">==<\/span><span class=\"st\">&#39;__main__&#39;<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-53\"><a href=\"#cb1-53\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> k <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">range<\/span>(COUNT): <span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> cpu_control(frame(k))<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>accel_control(frame(k))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-54\"><a href=\"#cb1-54\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> case <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> CASES:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-55\"><a href=\"#cb1-55\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> arch <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> (<span class=\"st\">&#39;CPU&#39;<\/span>,<span class=\"st\">&#39;HW&#39;<\/span>):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-56\"><a href=\"#cb1-56\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            rows<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>simulate(arch,case)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-57\"><a href=\"#cb1-57\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> [r[<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>] <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> r <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows]<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>tick_reference(arch,case)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-58\"><a href=\"#cb1-58\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            m<span class=\"op\">=<\/span>metrics(rows,case)<span class=\"op\">;<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> m[<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">+<\/span>m[<span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>]<span class=\"op\">==<\/span>COUNT<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-59\"><a href=\"#cb1-59\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            <span class=\"bu\">print<\/span>(case[<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>],arch,<span class=\"op\">*<\/span>[<span class=\"ss\">f&#39;<\/span><span class=\"sc\">{<\/span>x<span class=\"sc\">:.2f}<\/span><span class=\"ss\">&#39;<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">isinstance<\/span>(x,<span class=\"bu\">float<\/span>) <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> x <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> x <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> m])<\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Results and decision<\/h2>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-8\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-8\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-11\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-11\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-11\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-11\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-11\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-11\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-11\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scenario (P/D in µs)<\/th>\n<th>Path<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Completed<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Dropped<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Late<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Mean / max. (µs)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">CPU (%)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">DMA (B)<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Jobs/s<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Nominal operation (1000/700)<\/td>\n<td>CPU<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">555.00 / 555<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">55.50<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1000.00<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Nominal operation (1000/700)<\/td>\n<td>HW<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">218.00 / 218<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">7.30<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">13200<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1000.00<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CPU interference (1000/700)<\/td>\n<td>CPU<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">20<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">625.00 / 905<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">55.50<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1000.00<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CPU interference (1000/700)<\/td>\n<td>HW<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">288.00 / 568<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">7.30<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">13200<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1000.00<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bus interference (1000/700)<\/td>\n<td>CPU<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">555.00 / 555<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">55.50<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1000.00<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bus interference (1000/700)<\/td>\n<td>HW<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">20<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">338.00 / 818<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">7.30<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">13200<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1000.00<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>High rate (400/400)<\/td>\n<td>CPU<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">73<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">27<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">73<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">902.12 / 1105<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100.00<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1801.80<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>High rate (400/400)<\/td>\n<td>HW<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">218.00 / 218<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">18.25<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">13200<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2500.00<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Overload (180/180)<\/td>\n<td>CPU<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">34<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">66<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">34<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1003.68 / 1110<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100.00<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1801.80<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Overload (180/180)<\/td>\n<td>HW<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">83<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">17<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">83<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">342.51 / 434<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">33.49<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">10956<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">4587.16<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Combined (400/400)<\/td>\n<td>CPU<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">67<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">33<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">67<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">996.87 / 1260<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">92.53<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">1667.29<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Combined (400/400)<\/td>\n<td>HW<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">100<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">20<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">321.60 / 568<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">18.25<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">13200<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">2500.00<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>Under nominal conditions both variants meet the objective; the\nhardware variant reduces response time and the useful CPU time\npercentage, but requires an additional data path. CPU interference\ncauses 20 missed deadlines on the CPU variant, while the hardware\nvariant remains on time in the model. Bus interference has the opposite\neffect: only the accelerator path uses the DMA route considered here,\nand 20 jobs are late. At a release period of 400 µs, only the\naccelerator without additional interference reliably meets the deadline\nfor every modelled job. At 180 µs both serial servers are overloaded;\nneither assumed architecture meets the requirement. The combined\nworkload shows that a low nominal service time alone is\ninsufficient.<\/p>\n<p>The number of on-time responses is calculated as completed minus\nlate, not 100 minus late. Under overload it falls to zero for both\nvariants, in addition to the data losses. An alternative drop-old\nstrategy or an actual pipeline may change the age of responses, but\nrequires renewed interface and model verification. Energy, chip area and\nactual memory bandwidth have not been determined; a definitive hardware\ndecision is therefore not yet justified.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Further work and submission<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><strong>Boundary case:<\/strong> Change only the nominal case to a\nperiod of 555 µs and a deadline of 555 µs. <strong>Expected:<\/strong>\nthe CPU is exactly at the boundary, with all jobs on time in the absence\nof additional load and with correct handling of simultaneous events. Run\nboth models again.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><strong>Buffer:<\/strong> Increase the number of buffer slots to\nfour. <strong>Expected:<\/strong> temporarily fewer dropped jobs, but\npotentially longer response times; no lasting capacity gain under\nsustained overload.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><strong>Numerical arithmetic:<\/strong> Use a block consisting\nentirely of 0 or 4095 as a boundary test. <strong>Solution:<\/strong>\n4095 or 0, respectively; the implementations must agree. In an\nadditional hardware emulation, deliberately change the accumulator width\nto 16 bits and find a counterexample.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><strong>Hardware transfer:<\/strong> Define a future measurement\nprotocol with timestamps for release, DMA start, transfer completion,\ncomputation completion and output. Include buffer losses, measurement\nuncertainty and energy per job. Name the specific platform and\nconfiguration only once selected.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Submission: model parameters, unchanged reference program, six\nworkload variants for both architectures, table, latency/loss chart and\na justified decision for the specific workload. Software and hardware\narchitectures are equally valid design alternatives; the conclusion may\nalso be that neither meets the requirement.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.vvz.ethz.ch/Vorlesungsverzeichnis/sucheLehrangebot.view?abschnittId=122815&amp;ansicht=1&amp;lang=en&amp;seite=0&amp;semkez=2026W\">ETH\nZürich – Computers and Networks (Curriculum G5)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Autumn 2026,\nComputers and Networks track: 227-0124-00L Embedded Systems; curricular\ncomparison only, no proof of individual equations or experiment. · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://idsc.ethz.ch/education/lectures/embedded-control-systems.html\">ETH\nZürich – Embedded Control Systems, Institute for Dynamic Systems and\nControl<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Abstract and Subjects covered in lectures and practical\nlab exercises: sampling, ADC and timer interrupts; curricular context,\nnot evidence of project results. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-004-computation-structures-spring-2009/pages/lecture-notes/\">MIT\nOCW – 6.004, Lecture Notes: Pipelining, Memory Hierarchy, Parallel\nProcessing<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Lectures 8, 15–16, 19, 22–24: latency, memory\nhierarchy, interrupts and pipelining; no experiment validation. · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://docs.kernel.org/6.12/core-api/dma-api-howto.html\">Linux\nKernel – Dynamic DMA mapping Guide (6.12)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · CPU and DMA addresses\nsection: address spaces and DMA mapping on Linux; further-reading\nspecial case. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://documentation-service.arm.com/static/62a304f231ea212bb662321d\">Arm\n– Memory Systems, Ordering, and Barriers, v1.0 (PDF)<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · §§ 5–6,\npp. 12–14: DMB and DSB, ordering and completion of memory accesses;\nsupplementary architecture background. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>"};
